n":0.0051200003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Entegris, Inc. provides advanced materials and process solutions for the semiconductor and other high-technology industries in North America, Taiwan, South Korea, Japan, China, Europe, and Southeast Asia. It operates in two segments, Materials Solutions (MS) and Advanced Purity Solutions (APS). The MS segment provides materials-based solutions, such as chemical vapor and atomic layer deposition materials, chemical mechanical planarization slurries and pads, ion implantation specialty gases, formulated etch and clean materials, and other specialty materials. The APS segment offers filtration, purification, and contamination-control solutions for the semiconductor manufacturing processes, semiconductor ecosystem, and other high-technology industries. The company's customers include logic and memory semiconductor device manufacturers, semiconductor equipment makers, gas and chemical manufacturing companies, and wafer grower companies; and outsourced semiconductor assembly and test facilities, flat panel display equipment makers, and manufacturers of hard disk drive components and devices. It serves manufacturers and suppliers in the solar and life science industries, electrical discharge machining customers, glass manufacturers, aerospace manufacturers, and manufacturers of biomedical implantation devices. Entegris, Inc. was founded in 1966 and is headquartered in Billerica, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David W. Reeder | CEO, President & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $998,662 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $415K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $51K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Entegris, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $19.6B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $396M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 107% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0741635186821767},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (47% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Entegris (ENTG) Lifts Fourth Quarter Outlook As Valuation Debate Heats Up","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-entg/entegris/news/entegris-entg-lifts-fourth-quarter-outlook-as-valuation-deba","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793554163.224,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.842,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (ENTG)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_ENTG_110126011002_1793509802.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793509802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ENTG Q3 deep dive: manufacturing execution and content expansion drive outperformance","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/entg-q3-deep-dive-manufacturing-174729462.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793468849.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875